        "content": "<p>Wu's Characteristic Set Method has been well-known for automated theorem proving in geometry and polynomial system solving.</p>\n<p>We have formalized Wu's method in Lean 4, including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Triangulated set,</li>\n<li>Ascending set,</li>\n<li>Basic set,</li>\n<li>Pseudo-division of multivariate polynomials,</li>\n<li>Characteristic set,</li>\n<li>Zero decomposition algorithm, with the proof of <strong>Zero Decomposition Theorem</strong> over fields:  <br>\n    <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">D</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mtext>InitialProd</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Zero(PS) = \\bigcup_{CS \\in \\mathcal{ZD}} Zero(CS / \\text{InitialProd}(CS))</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07153em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ero</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05764em;\">PS</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0771em;vertical-align:-0.3271em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">⋃</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1786em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.05764em;\">CS</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">∈</span><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.07944em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mord mathcal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">D</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3271em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.07153em;\">Z</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ero</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05764em;\">CS</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">InitialProd</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05764em;\">CS</span><span class=\"mclose\">))</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Our project can be found at <a href=\"https://github.com/WuProver/lean_characteristic_set\">github.com/WuProver/lean_characteristic_set</a>, and we plan to gradually submit pull requests to Mathlib to upstream what we have completed.  <br>\nWe will be grateful for any reviews, remarks, and suggestions.</p>\n<p>Main contributor: <a href=\"https://github.com/SnkXyx\">@SnkXyx (Yuxuan Xiao)</a><br>\nOther contributors: <a href=\"https://github.com/tsuki8\">@tsuki8 (Hao Shen)</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/dingkang-wang\">@dingkang-wang (Dingkang Wang)</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/lzhimmrc\">@lzhimmrc (Lihong Zhi)</a></p>",
